## What this predicate means

**A `realizes` B** — A makes B concrete / actual.  Where B is an abstract concept (specification, plan, idea, design), A is its instantiated form.

Adjacent to `implements:` but broader:
- `implements:` — realization of a CONTRACT / interface / protocol
- `realizes:` — realization of ANY abstraction (idea, design, vision, plan)

Common shapes:
- A library realizes a design memorial
- A working session realizes a plan
- A code artifact realizes an architectural pattern
- A working session realizes an idea

